# The SDK this transport is built on lives in the org's registry on GitHub
# Packages. This line says where the scope lives; the token that authenticates
# the request does not belong in a committed file.
#
# GitHub Packages wants a token on every npm request — a public package there
# is readable by any account, but not anonymously. Provide one out of band, in
# your user-level ~/.npmrc, which keeps it out of the repository entirely:
#
#   //npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=<a token with read:packages>
#
# CI passes the same thing as NODE_AUTH_TOKEN, and the image build takes it as
# a BuildKit secret.
@assistant-hub-swarm:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
